WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.690
A heroic image puts the leader at the center of every success.

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:10.158
Shared or distributed leadership recognizes that influence and expertise can come from several people.

3
00:00:10.358 --> 00:00:18.337
At Cedar Crossing, a colleague with audio experience might guide a technical decision while another leads discussion of local sources.

4
00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:21.741
Sharing leadership still requires clear authority and support.

5
00:00:21.941 --> 00:00:31.399
Transactional leadership emphasizes exchanges and agreed performance; transformational leadership emphasizes shared purpose, development, and change.

6
00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.088
They are not simply bad and good alternatives.

7
00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:43.643
Collins's Level Five leadership combines personal humility with professional will, directing ambition toward the organization rather than personal acclaim.

8
00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:49.825
Treat that research-based description as a lens, not a promise that one personality guarantees success.

9
00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:52.260
Also attend to harmful behavior.

10
00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:59.003
Repeated humiliation, intimidation, or suppression of concerns can damage trust and information sharing.

11
00:00:59.203 --> 00:01:04.541
Toxic leadership concerns patterns and effects; a disagreement alone does not establish it.

12
00:01:04.741 --> 00:01:11.377
Invite informed challenge, give credit accurately, and make it possible to raise concerns through appropriate channels.
